Archie: create profiles locally without a sign-in step.

The profile picker offers "Sign in" as the first step of adding a
profile unless the BrowserSignin policy disables it. Treat "no policy"
as disabled so "Add profile" goes straight to naming and theming a
local profile. An explicit BrowserSignin policy is still honoured.

--- a/chrome/browser/ui/webui/signin/profile_picker_ui.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/webui/signin/profile_picker_ui.cc
@@ -72,7 +72,7 @@
       policy::key::kBrowserSignin, base::Value::Type::INTEGER);
 
   if (!browser_signin_value) {
-    return true;
+    return false;
   }
 
   return static_cast<policy::BrowserSigninMode>(
